    "summary": "I built a one-cell storage box. It has a full hex base with a full-depth bin inside, and a full cover on top as the lid. The lid is held shut by magnets: the parts list includes 6 neodymium disc magnets (Ø5 × 1 mm) and 6 steel BBs that they grip onto. The magnets were already on for this cover, so I didn't change any setting. I also added a trinity handle on the lid so you can lift it off. All open side faces have solid edge caps, and the joints are locked. The build check passed with no rule issues and no collisions between parts. In total it's 19 printed parts, about 687 g of filament and roughly 984 minutes of printing. I didn't add any props, since the brief didn't ask for any.",
